      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Ian speaks about the factors that are making ubiquitous virtualization possible, as well as its advantages.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Hypervisors are set to become ubiquitous on PC hardware, built-in to every server, and ultimately, every laptop too.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.xensource.com/&#34;&gt;open source Xen hypervisor&lt;/a&gt; is at the forefront of this movement, its architecture making it ideally suited for embedding in firmware and providing highly secure and efficient virtualization.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This talk looks at the hardware and software factors that are making ubiquitous virtualization possible, and discusses the benefits that virtualization brings to both data centres and personal computing devices.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Pratt will give a status update of the Xen project, and talk about some of the&#xA;cool new things that are on the roadmap.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
